WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:03.864
Here we improve our billing case expression by
adding a special category

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:10.089
for an exact zero The order is important First

00:00:10.296 --> 00:00:14.898
check for null Second check for zero and label it No
Charge

00:00:16.314 --> 00:00:21.560
Then check the High Value threshold After that check
the Standard threshold

00:00:23.054 --> 00:00:28.561
Finally use Low Value for the remaining known
amounts The complete

00:00:28.587 --> 00:00:33.035
query is available in the code cell Before running
it predict what

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:38.381
will happen to zero five thousand ten thousand and
null Then click

00:00:38.407 --> 00:00:42.906
Run in the browser and verify your predictions You
can also copy

00:00:42.932 --> 00:00:47.893
the SQL into pgAdmin This is a good example of
boundary testing

00:00:48.808 --> 00:00:52.726
The exact values at the edges of categories deserve
special attention
